      "ogDescription": "2 escudos de oro acuñados a máquina en Santa Fe de Bogotá en 1791, con el busto transicional de Carlos III bajo la leyenda de Carlos IV.",
      "template": "<div lang=\"en\" style=\"width:100%; min-height:100vh; background:#0a0a09; font-family:'Cormorant Garamond', serif; box-sizing:border-box;\">\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  <main data-pagefind-meta=\"url:/en/collection/spanish-colonial-coinage/2-escudos-carlos-iv-1791/\" id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 24px 80px; outline:none;\">\n\n    <a href=\"/en/collection/spanish-colonial-coinage/\" style=\"display:inline-block; color:#e7ddc4; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.08em; margin-bottom:24px;\">&larr; Spanish colonial coin catalog</a>\n\n    <div style=\"background:#d8d2cd; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.08); border-radius:3px; padding:clamp(28px,4vw,64px); box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);\">\n\n      <div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:760px; margin:0 auto 48px;\">\n        <span style=\"display:block; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; margin-bottom:14px;\">Spanish Colonial Coin &middot; Viceroyalty of New Granada &middot; Reign of Charles IV (1788&ndash;1808)</span>\n        <h1 style=\"font-family:'Montenegrin Gothic One', serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,46px); line-height:1.08; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1c1a15; margin:0 0 12px;\">2 Gold Escudos &mdash; 1791</h1>\n        <p style=\"font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px); font-style:italic; color:#4a4331; margin:0;\">Transitional bust &middot; Mint of Santa Fe de Bogotá (NR)</p>\n      </div>\n<div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">\n<button\n            data-zoom-trigger=\"carlos-iv-1791\"\n            aria-label=\"Enlarge imagen de los 2 escudos de 1791\"\n            style=\"all:unset; display:block; width:100%; position:relative; cursor:zoom-in; background:#1c1a15; border-radius:4px; padding:24px;\"\n          >\n            <picture>\n              <source srcset=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-carlos-iv-1791-bogota.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n              <img\n                src=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-carlos-iv-1791-bogota.jpg\"\n                alt=\"Gold 2-escudo of Charles IV, Bogotá 1791 — obverse with the transitional bust of Charles III (left) and reverse with the crowned royal coat of arms (right)\"\n                width=\"564\"\n                height=\"293\"\n                loading=\"eager\"\n                decoding=\"async\"\n                style=\"display:block; width:100%; height:auto;\"\n              />\n            </picture>\n            <span style=\"position:absolute; bottom:22px; right:22px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.82); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; padding:8px 14px; border-radius:999px;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; background:#d8d2cd; transform:rotate(45deg);\"></span>Enlarge</span>\n          </button>\n          <span style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:#5c4e33; text-align:center; font-style:italic;\">Obverse (left) and reverse (right) — Notofilia.com Collection</span>\n</div>\n\n      <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.75; color:#332e22; max-width:760px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">A piece of particular numismatic interest: although the legend names<strong>Carlos IV</strong>(&ldquo;CAROL. IV&rdquo;), the portrait on the obverse preserves the bust of his father,<strong>Carlos III</strong>. In the early years of a new reign, colonial mints used to continue to use the bust of the deceased king along with the name of the new monarch while the new official stamps arrived from Spain, &mdash;, an &ldquo;bridge&rdquo; piece between two reigns.</p>\n\n      <section id=\"2-escudos-1791\" style=\"max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;\">\n\n        <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 0 40px;\">\n          \n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column;\">\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Country / Viceroyalty</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">New Kingdom of Granada (present-day Colombia)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Mint / Assayer</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Santa Fe de Bogotá (brand &ldquo;NR&rdquo;) &middot; Assayer JJ (Juan de Dios del Real and José Antonio Rodríguez)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Reign</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Carlos IV (1788&ndash;1808)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Year of minting</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">1791</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Denomination</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">2 Gold Escudos</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Composition</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Gold .875 (21 carats)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Gross weight</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">6.75 g (mint standard specification)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Fine gold content</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">0.1901 troy oz (~5.91 g pure gold)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Diameter</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">~22 mm</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Manufacturing Method</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Machine minting (flywheel press)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Edge</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Cord (engraved edge against gold trim)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Catalog references</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">KM #51.1 &middot; Restrepo M88 &middot; Friedberg Fr-47 &middot; Numista N# 52841</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n\n          \n            <div\n              role=\"dialog\"\n              aria-modal=\"true\"\n              aria-label=\"Enlarged 2 escudos de 1791\"\n              data-zoom-dialog=\"carlos-iv-1791\" hidden\n             \n             class=\"catalog-zoom-dialog\">\n              <button\n                data-zoom-close\n                aria-label=\"Close\"\n                style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; right:28px; background:transparent; border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.4); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:22px; line-height:1; width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:50%; cursor:pointer;\"\n              >&times;</button>\n\n              <div style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; left:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.5); border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.25); border-radius:999px; padding:6px;\">\n                <button disabled=\"true\" aria-label=\"Zoom out\" style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\">&minus;</button>\n                <span style=\"min-width:56px; text-align:center; font-size:14px; color:#e7ddc4; letter-spacing:0.05em;\">100%</span>\n                <button disabled=\"false\" aria-label=\"Zoom in\" style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\">&#43;</button>\n              </div>\n\n              <div\n                style=\"overflow:hidden; max-width:92vw; max-height:74vh; touch-action:none;\"\n              >\n                <picture>\n                  <source srcset=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-carlos-iv-1791-bogota.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n                  <img\n                    src=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-carlos-iv-1791-bogota.jpg\"\n                    alt=\"2 escudos de oro de Carlos IV, Bogotá 1791, enlarged view\"\n                    draggable=\"false\"\n                    style=\"display:block; max-width:92vw; max-height:74vh; width:auto; height:auto; transform:; cursor:zoom-in; user-select:none;\"\n                  />\n                </picture>\n              </div>\n\n              <span style=\"margin-top:18px; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:#b7ab8a; font-style:italic;\">Drag to move &middot; Mouse wheel to zoom</span>\n            </div>\n          \n        </div>\n\n        \n\n        <section style=\"margin-top:44px;\">\n          <h3 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Obverse and Reverse</h3>\n          <ul style=\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px;\">\n            <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Obverse &mdash; The Bust:</strong>bust of Charles III, clothed and armored, facing right (the &ldquo;transitional bust&rdquo;). Legend:<em>CAROL. IV. D.G. HISP. ET IND. R.</em>(&ldquo;Carlos IV, by the Grace of God, King of Spain and the Indies&rdquo;). The date &ldquo;1791&rdquo; is centered under the bust.</span>\n            </li>\n            <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Reverse &mdash; The Crowned Shield:</strong>crowned royal coat of arms of Spain, surrounded by the collar of the Order of the Golden Fleece. Legend:<em>IN. UTROQ. FELIX. AUSPICE. DEO</em>(&ldquo;In both worlds, happy under the guidance of God&rdquo;). The coat of arms is flanked by the name &ldquo;2&rdquo; (left) and &ldquo;S&rdquo; (right), and in the lower register, the mint mark &ldquo;NR&rdquo; (Nuevo Reino, Bogotá) and the assayer's initials &ldquo;JJ&rdquo;.</span>\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </section>\n\n      </section>\n\n      <blockquote style=\"max-width:760px; margin:56px auto 0; padding:28px 0 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.15);\">\n        <p style=\"font-size:20px; font-style:italic; line-height:1.7; color:#4a4331; margin:0 0 10px;\">This 1791 piece belongs to the mechanized era of Santa Fe, which began after the expansion of the Mint in 1756 and the general adoption of flywheel presses in 1757. Its round shape, uniform thickness and corded edge contrast with the old hammer macuquinas. The bust of Charles III under the legend of Charles IV also makes it a bridge between two reigns.</p>\n        <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:#5c4e33;\">&mdash; Historical Context Note</span>\n      </blockquote>\n\n      <section style=\"max-width:760px; margin:32px auto 0; padding-top:24px; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n        <h2 style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 12px; font-style:normal;\">Sources</h2>\n        <ul style=\"margin:0; padding:0 0 0 20px; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; color:#5c4e33; font-style:italic;\">\n          <li>Restrepo Restrepo, José Ignacio.<em>Two Hundred Years of Republican Currency in Colombia (1810–2010)</em>— base reference for the Restrepo number.</li>\n          <li>Krause, Chester L. y Clifford Mishler.<em>Standard Catalog of World Coins.</em></li>\n          <li>Numista —<a href=\"https://en.numista.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">numista.com<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>\n          <li>Rodríguez Soage, José David.<a href=\"https://www.enumismatic.com/mints-history/santa-fe/es/la-ceca-de-santa-fe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">&laquo;The Santa Fe Mint&raquo;<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a>, eNumismatic, 2021.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </section>\n\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  \n\n</div>",
      "recordTitle": "2 Escudos de Oro — 1791",
      "eyebrow": "Moneda Colonial Española · Virreinato de la Nueva Granada · Reinado de Carlos IV (1788&ndash;1808)"
